{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"drastic-flattish-rodent","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Live capture (2026-08-06, reported by a second session attempting to certify c9f7-d6df-bce0-4b77): THREE byte-identical gate_error_v1 sidecars on c9f7, cause \"step 'decide@then/verify' failed: completion recovery context bound exceeded\", diagnostic stage=preflight, context_chars=121147, context_char_limit=100000, criteria_total=22, criteria_completed=0. The primary verifier handled the 121k context fine (it failed by LOOPING — aggregate_exception_type=RunawayToolLoopError, abort at 55 requests, distinct_ratio_window=0.5, search_files x11 — the c827 actuator working as designed); ONLY the recovery preflight refuses. A retry can never succeed: the store is append-only (no comment delete — pinned by test_completion_recovery_oversized_d59e.py's own docstring), so the context only grows. The sole documented exit is --force-close: the exhaustion-is-not-a-verdict trap, third form (after the c827 loop burnouts and ed6d's evidence-run death).\n\nThis is the SECOND outgrowth of the flat bound: d59e raised 24,000 -> 100,000 when ticket 9fd4 (34,282 chars) was refused, with 2.4x headroom over the largest ticket then observed; c9f7 (121,092 chars = description 15,651 + 10 comments totaling 105,053, of which ONE plan-review remediation comment is 99,009) blew through it within weeks. A flat per-context bound chases a monotonically growing tail.\n\nRoot cause: _MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS conflates two different ceilings. (1) Physical: each evidence run must fit the context in one model window. (2) Economic: recovery re-sends the context once PER criterion, so recovery spend scales with context_chars x criteria_count; 100,000 was chosen to keep the worst case at _MAX_CRITERIA (32) x 100k = 3.2M chars. c9f7's actual recovery input (22 x 121,147 = 2.67M chars) is UNDER that already-ratified worst case — it is refused only because the per-axis split is arbitrary.\n\nPlan: express the two ceilings directly in _validate_recovery_inputs (completion_recovery.py):\n- Raise _MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS from 100_000 to 400_000 — the physical ceiling (~100k tokens, fits the 200k-token model window with headroom for the system prompt, criterion, and output).\n- Add _MAX_RECOVERY_INPUT_CHARS = 3_200_000 and refuse when len(context) * len(criteria) exceeds it — the economic ceiling, byte-identical to the previously ratified worst case (32 x 100k), now allocated where real tickets need it instead of split per-axis.\n- Refusal stays elision-free and visible, with diagnostic {context_chars, criteria_total, recovery_input_chars, recovery_input_char_limit}.\n- d59e's pinned invariants are preserved: nothing is ever elided (the full context reaches the model byte-identical), the criteria budget (32,000) stays <= the context budget, and an over-budget payload still refuses with zero billable calls.\n\nOut of scope, filed separately: write-time comment-size hygiene (the 99k scanner dump belongs in a session log, not a comment) and context-first evidence-instruction ordering to exploit provider prompt caching across the N per-criterion re-sends.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The live c9f7 shape is accepted: _validate_recovery_inputs with a 121,147-char context and 22 criteria proceeds to the first evidence run, with zero runner calls made before it (unit test, held-out oracle style).\n- [ ] The physical ceiling holds: a context over 400,000 chars is refused with CompletionRecoveryError carrying {context_chars, context_char_limit} before any runner call (unit test).\n- [ ] The economic ceiling holds: a context x criteria product over 3,200,000 is refused with CompletionRecoveryError carrying {context_chars, criteria_total, recovery_input_chars, recovery_input_char_limit} before any runner call (unit test).\n- [ ] d59e's pinned invariants stay green: the full context reaches the model byte-identical (nothing elided), _MAX_TOTAL_CRITERIA_CHARS <= _MAX_CONTEXT_CHARS still holds, and the over-budget refusal makes zero billable calls (existing d59e tests pass with constants updated only where they name the old bound).\n- [ ] Live Bedrock proof before ship: a synthetic ticket whose assembled context exceeds 100,000 chars completes bounded recovery to a verdict under a forced-low primary budget, instead of refusing at preflight (session experiment, not in unit suite; result recorded on this ticket).\n- [ ] From a fixed checkout, a completion verification of c9f7-d6df-bce0-4b77 no longer emits the \"completion recovery context bound exceeded\" gate_error_v1: either the primary lands a verdict or recovery proceeds past preflight into evidence runs (recorded on this ticket; the verdict's PASS/FAIL merits are out of scope).\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck pass; the unit marker suite matches the pre-existing baseline.\n\n## Testing\nHeld-out unit oracle written RED-first: new tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_recovery_context_product_bound.py for the two-ceiling contract, plus constant updates in test_completion_recovery_oversized_d59e.py. Run: python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/ -q. Live Bedrock experiments per the two live ACs recorded as ticket comments. make lint + make typecheck.","id":"8eb3-1f20-f395-4ea5","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Recovery context bound refuses c9f7 forever (121k > 100k): flat bound outgrown a second time"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785990144423024001,"uuid":"9893a3d3-f799-42a5-a791-5d291f983feb"}